A||||17||EdsB52||Skydiving||||1||
Z||000000||EdsB52||10-28-2001||10:38 PM||||Anybody try skydiving? I had 3 static lines from several years ago and decidied to continue with a tandem form 13,000 agl. What a frickin rush. I'm going to get licensed. You ought to see the puss that skydives; I didn't think there was that much scratch that participated in dangerous activities like that.<P>You want to see the dangerousness surrounding skydiving? Check this out:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.skydivenet.com/fatalities/fatalities_us_01.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.skydivenet.com/fatalities/fatalities_us_01.html</A> <P>||||reg||1
Z||000001||maryjane||10-28-2001||11:03 PM||||always wondered why they called it skydiving.<BR>It's earth you dive towards. Only did it once, long ago. The first 10 feet were the worst.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000002||Nashco||10-28-2001||11:18 PM||||I really really want to get into it.  A guy I go to school with has gone through all the beginner levels, and the price per jump was a lot lower than I had expected.  He's got a parachute folding certification now, and that's how he pays for his jumps.  He shows up at the beginning of the day, folds enough parachutes to pay for a jump on the "up high" plane, makes his jump, then comes on home.  I would love an opportunity to do this..just go let off some steam on the weekend if I needed to!  I will probably do it with some friends (all our first times) next summer, we all want to do it badly!  I can't wait <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||GarethWright||10-29-2001||12:21 AM||||I had a friend in High School that would literally spend All weekend skydiving, he packed enough parachutes between jumps that he earned money doing it!  When he went off to the Air Force (para-rescue) he had done over 175 jumps.  I went out with him a few times, but only did static line from 4k, a real rush, but the price tends to add up.||||reg||1
Z||000004||EdsB52||10-29-2001||12:56 AM||||"always wondered why they called it skydiving. It's earth you dive towards."<P>Really!!! Actually gravity predicates which way you go, even if you were to dive up.<P>Only did it once, long ago. The first 10 feet were the worst.<P>In the military? And you're right, the initial acceleration is a rush. Once you stabilize, the only *****  is the difficulty breathing.<P>The rest of you guys should check it out. I wish I was 10 years younger so I could score on some of those sky bunnies. I have real respect for chicks that have the courage to do sh!t like this; most of the chicks I date are happy going shopping while me and my buddies go do crazy **** . Did you guys check out the web site? Pretty interesting, especially the suicides while skydiving.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Tonker||10-29-2001||12:31 PM||||Tried it once and loved it. It was awesome, we did a pilot chute jump, not static line, but it's basically the same. My buddies and I did it just after our BOTC course while we were on the West Coast for our First summer of training with the Naval Reserve. We decided we could be Canada's equivalent to the US Navy Seals.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000006||Ken Wittlief||10-29-2001||01:22 PM||||a guy I worked with went once - on his first jump (is that called a static dive, where the chute opens as you jump out?)<P> on his first jump his chute tangled. The instructor was on the ground screaming "CUT IT CUT IT CUT IT" into the headset radio<P> he had to cut the chute loose and pull the spare. It popped open about 3 seconds before he would have hit the ground, so his total time hanging from the chute was about 15 seconds.<P> He loved every second of it - what a rush! Now hes hooked.||||reg||1
Z||000007||1FST2M6||10-29-2001||01:39 PM||||i've got 11 jumps under my belt.. all done at North Carolina Sky Sports... fastest 14,000 foot decent i've ever done!! if you don't toss the drouge shoot and dive head first to T.V. your ears, and nose will bleed!!! I'TS GREAT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>skydiving is one thing EVERYONE should do at LEAST once in their life time!! <P>------------------<BR>0-60 in 4.91<P> <A HREF="http://www.1fst2m6.com" TARGET=_blank>www.1fst2m6.com</A>  - underconstruction - but check it out anywho...||||reg||1
Z||000008||JSocha||10-29-2001||02:39 PM||||My brother has skydived and loves it.  <P>Me, I prefer scuba diving anyday of the week, cause you know your too deep when strange fish start offering you candy and plus nobody can hear you scream at 200'.<P>So, just my thought on this...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"> Why jump out of a perfectly good airplane.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  <P>Or is there just no end to the madness/insanity?!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/jsocha_2.gif"> ||||reg||10
Z||000009||EdsB52||10-29-2001||04:27 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by JSocha:<BR><B>My brother has skydived and loves it.  <P><BR>So, just my thought on this...<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif">    <P>Or is there just no end to the madness/insanity?!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"Me, I prefer scuba diving anyday of the week, cause you know your too deep when strange fish start offering you candy and plus nobody can hear you scream at 200'."<P>LOL! Isn't 150ft the deepest you can go without decompression? I have 10 dives in the Marianas, off Guam. It's awesome diving there.<P>"Why jump out of a perfectly good airplane.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">"<P>Because they're not perfectly good! Incidents involving skydivers where the plane crashed and kill all on board aren't all that infrequent; most of the planes used are not perfectly good, although able to land.||||reg||1
Z||000010||EdsB52||10-29-2001||04:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>i've got 11 jumps under my belt.. all done at North Carolina Sky Sports... fastest 14,000 foot decent i've ever done!! if you don't toss the drouge shoot and dive head first to T.V. your ears, and nose will bleed!!! I'TS GREAT!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  <P>skydiving is one thing EVERYONE should do at LEAST once in their life time!! <P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Are you licensed? If not, are getting there? Are your dives recent or not? Why will your ears and nose bleed if you accelerate to TV w/o the drouge chute? Is it the rapid rate of descent?||||reg||1
Z||000011||1FST2M6||10-29-2001||04:45 PM||||nope straped to instructor for the first 6 then tied to a string for 2 now i've got instructor assisted free fall for 4 and i'm legal... (so one jump left) yeah fairly recent... a friend of mine that owned indexbbs.com died in a skydiving accident... he backed into the prop on a King air and the prop caught his chute and whiped him into the side of the plane. all on the ground.. we didn't dive the rest of the day... Rodney Aloia..  we miss ya man!  <P>you bleed cause the pressure outside of your nasal cavity changes to fast and the pressure inside can't equalize as fast.. that inaddition to the wind pressure beating on the same passages, kinda like decompression SCUBA diving but not as dangerous. (i've got my PADI openwater certification too.. that came in handy on my honeymoon in Jamaica in May) the classes counted tward my ME degree too!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000012||fogglethorpe||10-29-2001||05:21 PM||||No, no, no...<BR>Terra Firma and me are buds.||||reg||1
Z||000013||hugh||10-29-2001||05:39 PM||||Me too,the more firma,the less terra!||||reg||1
Z||000014||JSocha||10-29-2001||05:44 PM||||Ed, That's why at 200', noone can hear you scream!  <P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"> If those strange fish offering candy at that depth aren't the hint your just a little deeper then you should be, your SOL!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_brow.gif"><P>Nitrogen Narcosis is only fun for so long.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><P>Been down beyond my recreational limit of 100'.  Had no choice.  Another diver who was in my group as I was group leader two years ago for a dive trip up to Canada, his brand new BC failed and after 60+' he dropped like a rock past our group and he couldn't inflate and he didn't drop his weights.  <P>The rest of the group stayed at 60-65' where I indicated for them to level off at, wait 5 minutes and if I wasn't back within that time to surface as I had to go after him.  Good thing our group went over signals.  Found him between 150-175' still going down the mud slope, and slowly took him up using my BC and the weights to compensate for the extra time we needed to decompress.||||reg||12
Z||000015||EdsB52||10-29-2001||08:35 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>nope straped to instructor for the first 6 then tied to a string for 2 now i've got instructor assisted free fall for 4 and i'm legal... (so one jump left) yeah fairly recent... a friend of mine that owned indexbbs.com died in a skydiving accident... he backed into the prop on a King air and the prop caught his chute and whiped him into the side of the plane. all on the ground.. we didn't dive the rest of the day... Rodney Aloia..  we miss ya man!  <P>you bleed cause the pressure outside of your nasal cavity changes to fast and the pressure inside can't equalize as fast.. that inaddition to the wind pressure beating on the same passages, kinda like decompression SCUBA diving but not as dangerous. (i've got my PADI openwater certification too.. that came in handy on my honeymoon in Jamaica in May) the classes counted tward my ME degree too!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Is this the incident to which you are referring?<P>"Date Location Category Age # Jumps AAD?/RSL? <BR>5/27/01 San Marcos, TX BIZ, AIR 36 850+ ??/?? <BR>Description: This jumper was participating in a 30-way skydive, exiting from a King Air, which was to be flying trail behind an Otter. She was somewhere in the middle of the exit lineup in the king air. At exit time, however, the king air ended up in front and above the otter. This jumper, shortly after exiting the King Air, struck the propeller of the Otter. One camera man observed this jumper spinning out of control, and went twice for the reserve handle, succeeding on the 2nd attempt. The reserve, however, did not deploy correctly, as it had been badly damaged during the collision. The cameraman landed covered in blood etc. She landed off the DZ in a yard, and her significant other landed nearby. She was pronounced DOA by the corner, having been seriously injured from the chest up by the prop-strike. There is an NTSB report of this incident at: <A HREF="http://www.ntsb.gov/ntsb/brief.asp?ev_id=20010601X01046&key=1" TARGET=_blank>http://www.ntsb.gov/ntsb/brief.asp?ev_id=20010601X01046&key=1</A>  <BR>Lessons:  This is a unique event. King Air's can fly at a higher airspeed than Twin Otters, and it is possible and error was made by either or both pilots when setting up the exit. However, the jumpers in the door of the King Air should have had visual contact with the Otter. Very likely, they exited the plane despite having the wrong configuration without considering the possibility of collision. Given that this has never happened before, it's not unreasonable to fail to consider this possibility when outside the door of the plane, ready to go. Certainly, this incident will be discussed widely, and hopefully jumpers will be encouraged to abort a skydive when presented with unfavorable positioning of the aircraft. ||||reg||1
Z||000016||TRiAD||10-30-2001||08:49 AM||||"It's not the long fall that bothers me, but the abrupt halt at the end."   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR><B><I>Michael ~ triadtuning@hotmail.com</I></B><BR>-----------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88FieroGTwhitefscustomcroppedmini.jpg">   <IMG SRC="http://communities.msn.com/_Secure/0NgAlAL0S2vLvViYU9P7uloj72fLFTqfz59trng8I7AOG7hGCvfk6WP96n!gnOaEUAvooy1kUoWucv7BJ7L5EWg/temp-sig.gif">    <BR><I>Photoshop rendering of planned exterior modifications.</I>||||reg||1
Z||000017||yo_sweets_babe||10-31-2001||07:55 PM||||i was gonna go for my first jump just this past summer but they wouldn't let me cuz i'm only 15 so they're making me wait till next summer....grrrrrrr<P>i've white water rafted n bunjee jumped so i don't see what was so wrong about this...||||reg||9
